    <briefdescription>
<para>Indicates that an LE credit-based connection response is received. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Result code <ref refid="group__sl__bt__l2cap_1ggae9842dbd44c2e083436b58bcd06cdb42ac9cf1e0fa42f9d334727f0a95c63905a" kindref="member">sl_bt_l2cap_connection_result_successful</ref> in <computeroutput>errorcode</computeroutput> implies that the logical channel is established and data can be sent or received on the channel.</para>
<para>If the connection request was rejected by the peer, indicated by <computeroutput>errorcode</computeroutput>, the stack automatically closes the local channel and the user application should clean up the resources associated to the channel identifier. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
